cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or adapt this code, please cite the paper and this repository."
type: software
title: "dihedral-hessenberg: Lean verification of Dot actions and Hessenberg spaces for dihedral groups"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of J. Boretsky, R. Hodges, N. Lesnevich, T. McAllister,
  J. Pappe, "Dot actions and Hessenberg spaces for dihedral groups": the
  freeness of the modules of splines of Hessenberg spaces for the dihedral
  groups, their rank generating functions and Hilbert series (Theorem 1); an
  explicit homogeneous flow-up basis (Theorem 2); and the left and right dot
  action representations in the graded representation ring (Theorem 3),
  together with every lemma, example and remark of the paper. Accompanying
  libraries develop generalized splines, the dihedral groups with their roots,
  invariant theory and representations, and graded characters of finite groups.
authors:
  - family-names: Hodges
    given-names: Reuven
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rhodges-math/dihedral-hessenberg"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formalization
  - generalized splines
  - dihedral groups
  - Hessenberg spaces
  - dot action
  - Coxeter groups
  - representation theory
